From: VIKINGYFY <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:57:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gc: retain failed deletions and protect referenced records

Whole-record GC currently drops database rows after external deletion
fails, omits tracked media, and can remove traces or threads that still
have live children.

Delete only successfully cleaned IDs and advance a bounded ID cursor so
failed rows remain retryable without blocking later batches. Load media
storage references, protect surviving executions and pending/processing
rows, and clean requests, traces and threads in child-to-parent order.

Share an admission lock across manual and scheduled GC. Bound cleanup
with configurable batch size, cancellable pacing and timeout. Propagate
cleanup errors, publish scheduler errors, and log completion and counts.

